WEBVTT

00:09.710 --> 00:11.710
<b>Breaking News: Shiga Train Derailment</b>

00:09.710 --> 00:11.710
<b>Recovery efforts continue</b>

00:14.750 --> 00:17.250
I hope Ai-chan's okay...

00:17.920 --> 00:20.420
Oh, right. I can just send her a message.

00:21.000 --> 00:24.000
<b>Hey, Ai-chan, how are you feeling?</b>

00:21.460 --> 00:23.170
She's bound to reply if she's feeling better.

00:24.000 --> 00:25.250
<b>Hey, Ai-chan,</b>

00:24.000 --> 00:25.250
<b>how are you feeling?</b>

00:25.250 --> 00:25.670
<b>Ai-chan</b>

00:26.210 --> 00:27.960
Ai-chan?! That was fast!

00:29.580 --> 00:31.170
Sensei!

00:31.170 --> 00:33.290
Ai-chan, what's wrong? Are you okay?!

00:34.790 --> 00:37.580
I got knocked out,
but I only ended up with a few scratches.

00:37.580 --> 00:39.630
I was so worried you were seriously hurt.

00:40.420 --> 00:41.330
Talk about lucky.

00:42.460 --> 00:44.460
Is it really, though?

00:46.420 --> 00:52.420
Because maybe that accident
only happened 'cause I was there,

00:52.750 --> 00:55.830
and all those people got hurt because I was there.

00:57.580 --> 01:00.500
I'm really unlucky.

01:01.040 --> 01:04.000
Me and everyone who hangs around me, too.

01:05.880 --> 01:09.000
What hospital are you at?

01:09.000 --> 01:09.790
Huh?

01:10.250 --> 01:13.710
Well, Yayoi-chan, Eiko,
and I want to come down and pay you a visit.

01:14.000 --> 01:18.420
I think you'll feel better
once you get to talk to some friends.

01:18.960 --> 01:21.500
Then, you'll see you're just overthinking things,
and it's not your fault.

01:21.500 --> 01:25.540
Okay, but what if seeing me
makes something bad happen again?

01:25.540 --> 01:29.750
We'll be okay. Yayoi-chan will be there.
God, that sounds so pathetic...

01:31.040 --> 01:34.210
And everyone's worried about you, Ai.

01:34.710 --> 01:37.540
We all just want to see you smile again!

01:44.080 --> 01:48.500
No one's ever said that to me before! Thank you!

01:48.830 --> 01:53.500
I'll be here! I can't wait to see you, Sensei!

01:53.630 --> 01:55.750
Same. We'll be there soon, okay?

01:56.670 --> 01:58.040
See you then.

01:58.040 --> 01:59.830
Right! Bye-bye!

02:01.170 --> 02:03.500
Gah! I forgot to get the name!

02:04.330 --> 02:05.630
<b>Kyoto Central Hospital</b>

02:05.790 --> 02:08.000
<b>So hype!</b>

02:09.210 --> 02:12.710
So I got the name of the hospital she's staying at.

02:13.080 --> 02:16.460
I was so excited to come in here and tell you, too...

02:16.790 --> 02:19.880
But now the school's closed
because of some crazy ghost incident?!

02:20.000 --> 02:23.000
And one of your classmates was replaced by a ghost
who's in league with other body-snatchers?

02:23.000 --> 02:25.750
AND they probably know our addresses?!

02:26.080 --> 02:28.880
I don’t even know where to start...

02:29.210 --> 02:31.630
Actually, how about with whatever the hell
you're doing, Eiko?!

02:31.630 --> 02:33.920
I'm putting up spy cameras!

02:33.920 --> 02:36.130
Obviously! You mind telling me WHY?!

02:36.130 --> 02:38.830
To catch a body-snatcher if they break in.

02:38.830 --> 02:39.920
Oh, really?!

02:40.000 --> 02:41.920
<b>KEI-KUN'S</b>

02:40.000 --> 02:41.920
<b>ROOM!</b>

02:40.000 --> 02:41.920
<b>CAMERA</b>

02:40.040 --> 02:41.830
Then why'd you put up this many?!

02:42.000 --> 02:45.290
You know I wish I didn't have to, but I had to. So I did!

02:45.710 --> 02:51.210
Y'know, sometimes, there are things
in this world you just can't avoid doing!

02:51.210 --> 02:52.420
Why're you so excited about it, then?

02:52.420 --> 02:54.250
I'm the only one who can see the feeds,

02:54.250 --> 02:59.540
and if things look sketchy,
I'll ask Shami-san's team to take care of it!

02:59.540 --> 03:01.040
O-okay...

03:01.420 --> 03:05.130
I didn't think things would go this far off the rails...

03:05.130 --> 03:08.920
In any case, everything's prepared for our trip to Kyoto.

03:09.250 --> 03:14.580
Our objective is to visit Ai,
then confront her god face-to-face.

03:14.960 --> 03:20.710
There's a 90% chance things get ugly, which means we'll
need to strategize and prepare before that confrontation.

03:20.920 --> 03:22.250
We need a plan...

03:22.790 --> 03:27.250
A while back, you said you'd taken on a god before.
How'd you do that?

03:27.670 --> 03:33.210
Simply put, it's a numbers game,
where you batter it with curses to keep weakening it.

03:29.170 --> 03:33.670
<b>GOD</b>

03:35.000 --> 03:38.500
Ai's god is far more powerful than I thought, however.

03:38.880 --> 03:44.130
Not only is it powerful on its own,
but it has a spirit to heal it and at least twelve lackies.

03:45.250 --> 03:48.750
I've come up with a plan to raise our odds of beating it.

03:49.630 --> 03:53.210
I'll spell it out for you two so we can fine-tune it together.

03:54.420 --> 03:57.710
Currently, we have seven graduates at our disposal.

03:58.540 --> 04:00.170
The High Priest of the Evil Tongue.

04:00.960 --> 04:02.880
The Imprisoned Martyr.

04:04.130 --> 04:06.130
Otogiri Oiran, the Soul-Sucking Courtesan.

04:07.420 --> 04:09.540
The Suicide at Sengon-Kegon Falls.

04:10.750 --> 04:14.540
The ghost from the Old Old F Tunnel,
The Faceless Fiend.

04:15.790 --> 04:19.830
The ghost from the Old I Watergate,
The Black Asura in Lunar Umbra.

04:20.460 --> 04:26.630
And the ghost that got stronger
during the incident at school, the Soul in Transition.

04:27.290 --> 04:32.000
Stories tell of an ancient exorcist
who placed a protective ward over all of Kyoto.

04:32.420 --> 04:38.000
We'll follow suit, reserving the Martyr
and the Oiran for their weakening abilities,

04:38.540 --> 04:44.250
then placing the other five in a pentagram
of Kyoto's most haunted locations.

04:44.630 --> 04:47.130
I call it: the Bellflower of Blasphemy.

04:47.830 --> 04:49.580
It will be the inverse of a ward,

04:49.790 --> 04:55.170
trapping the god inside to shrivel and weaken
at the hands of the Martyr and the Oiran.

04:55.670 --> 04:59.170
Once weakened enough, we retrieve our Graduates,

04:59.710 --> 05:02.920
then use our overwhelming numbers to take it down.

05:04.750 --> 05:08.750
So we'd be creating a curse that covers the entire city?

05:08.750 --> 05:09.500
Yup.

05:09.670 --> 05:13.880
But wouldn't that also affect everyone who lives there?

05:14.000 --> 05:15.670
It would, if we let it.

05:16.170 --> 05:19.710
But we won't, so we'll need two things:

05:20.290 --> 05:25.040
A substitute with the curse drawn onto it,
and a substitute for the city of Kyoto itself.

05:25.540 --> 05:27.790
Wait, how are we going to do that?!

05:27.790 --> 05:34.580
We grab soil or something from one part of the city
to fashion into the substitute.

05:34.960 --> 05:36.540
That transfers the curse away from the city.

05:37.380 --> 05:40.040
This substitute is the key.

05:40.580 --> 05:43.710
<b>TYPICAL</b>

05:40.880 --> 05:44.210
Usually, substitutes take damage intended for a human,

05:44.380 --> 05:48.790
<b>REVERSE</b>

05:44.420 --> 05:48.710
but this one works in reverse,
transferring damage from the city to the god.

05:49.130 --> 05:52.500
But how do we turn the god into a substitute?

05:52.500 --> 05:56.040
We mark it the same way.

05:56.380 --> 05:57.540
Mark it?

05:57.880 --> 06:00.250
Oh, with that symbol?

06:00.420 --> 06:05.040
Precisely. I came up with this symbol
so it's completely unique.

06:05.210 --> 06:09.630
We'll carve it into the god's flesh to make
a permanent link between it and the substitute.

06:10.040 --> 06:13.580
B-but wait, the god can heal itself, can't it?

06:16.210 --> 06:19.710
That's from Castle H. The Suicide's curse!

06:20.290 --> 06:27.670
That's right. She can inflict wounds that can't be healed,
and we can use her obi to strike it from out of range.

06:28.250 --> 06:31.630
O-okay, so how do these two things work together?

06:32.380 --> 06:33.830
Like this.

06:34.330 --> 06:39.500
We place the curse over Kyoto.
The effects get channeled into the city's substitute.

06:39.920 --> 06:46.830
Those flow through gravity down
into to substitute with the mark.

06:48.290 --> 06:54.130
That then transfers through
the Suicide's markings to the god,

06:54.540 --> 06:59.250
afflicting it with a curse powerful enough to level a city.

07:01.250 --> 07:04.460
I can't believe she came up with all of this...

07:04.790 --> 07:10.330
Got it! So the curse won't affect anyone else
except for the god!

07:10.330 --> 07:11.210
Yup.

07:11.210 --> 07:12.670
That's so cool!

07:12.920 --> 07:17.670
Okay, let's draw up what steps we need to take
to enact the plan and put it on a schedule.

07:17.670 --> 07:18.380
Mhmm.

07:19.040 --> 07:23.420
I assume the god will pick a fight with us
when we go to visit Ai-chan.

07:23.750 --> 07:26.420
So we want to finish most of our prep
before we go to see her.

07:24.830 --> 07:28.630
<b>May 7: Prep</b>

07:24.830 --> 07:28.630
<b>May 8: Drive from</b>

07:24.830 --> 07:28.630
<b>Tokyo to Kyoto</b>

07:24.840 --> 07:28.630
<b>May 8-10: Clear all five spots,</b>

07:24.840 --> 07:28.630
<b>set up Graduates</b>

07:24.840 --> 07:28.630
<b>May 10: Finish other prep</b>

07:24.840 --> 07:28.630
<b>(substitutes, etc.)</b>

07:24.840 --> 07:28.630
<b>May 11: Go visit Ai</b>

07:24.840 --> 07:28.630
<b>May 11: Confront God</b>

07:24.840 --> 07:28.630
<b>May 11-12: WIN</b>

07:27.130 --> 07:28.250
How's this look?

07:29.000 --> 07:30.080
Good.

07:30.080 --> 07:31.790
For prep, then...

07:32.000 --> 07:35.920
We'll need to hit five crucial spots
to make the pentagram.

07:36.330 --> 07:38.790
I've picked out these five.

07:39.000 --> 07:40.630
<b>F Park</b>

07:40.630 --> 07:42.250
<b>K-zuka Daimyojin Shrine</b>

07:42.250 --> 07:43.880
<b>T Tunnel</b>

07:43.880 --> 07:45.500
<b>A Dam</b>

07:45.500 --> 07:47.130
<b>National Highway Between OW and OT</b>

07:47.710 --> 07:49.000
That's Kyoto for you.

07:49.000 --> 07:53.250
A place so steeped in haunted history
was sure to have top-tier haunts,

07:53.250 --> 07:55.540
and none of them are going to be easy.

07:56.960 --> 08:01.630
We have to hit all these places before taking on the god?

08:01.630 --> 08:03.460
We could end up dead before that.

08:04.000 --> 08:08.040
True, but with great risk comes greater rewards.

08:08.250 --> 08:13.420
By securing each location for our Graduate,
we'll also capture powerful spirits.

08:15.960 --> 08:21.210
The god's lackies are less powerful than it,
but they'll still be a force to be reckoned with.

08:22.000 --> 08:23.960
We can't cut corners when it comes to them.

08:25.540 --> 08:27.710
Given the inherent danger of this plan,

08:28.460 --> 08:32.790
I want the two of you to really consider
whether or not you want to go to Kyoto.

08:33.830 --> 08:37.170
Your lives will truly be in danger
during the course of this battle.

08:37.500 --> 08:40.830
You could very well be throwing away everything
for the sake of one friend.

08:41.420 --> 08:45.790
You're well within your rights to freak out
and run away. That reaction is completely normal.

08:46.250 --> 08:51.710
So I want you to think long and hard about it,
then make a decision.

08:52.540 --> 08:56.080
If you still want to come,
then meet me here tomorrow morning.

09:09.330 --> 09:12.130
Hey, come on in!

09:13.630 --> 09:16.380
Why'd you ask me to bring you a ghost?

09:16.380 --> 09:19.210
Cause I want you to see something.

09:20.290 --> 09:21.210
What is it?

09:21.630 --> 09:23.130
You'll see.

09:23.580 --> 09:26.210
I just don't know if it'll attack, so be on your guard.

09:29.920 --> 09:32.920
Is that the girl from the F Tunnel?

09:33.040 --> 09:33.830
Yep.

09:34.380 --> 09:42.420
I upgraded the design, so no matter
what damage it takes, it'll always regenerate.

09:42.630 --> 09:45.080
I call it the "self-sustaining substitute."

09:46.290 --> 09:47.460
Is it too creepy?

09:49.630 --> 09:51.960
I can't believe you're already thinking about this, too!

09:53.330 --> 09:56.250
Uh, that wasn't the reaction I was expecting...

09:56.250 --> 09:58.710
I had the same idea before.

09:59.710 --> 10:03.420
But I abandoned it, since I wanted to train them instead.

10:04.330 --> 10:09.080
You put this together right after getting a ghost, too.
I need to hire you as my assistant.

10:09.670 --> 10:10.750
Professor!

10:11.130 --> 10:13.250
For now, let me repair the paper substitute.

10:13.250 --> 10:14.290
Wait!

10:15.000 --> 10:19.330
That would help, but that's not why
I asked you to come here.

10:24.750 --> 10:26.040
What's in the closet?

10:27.040 --> 10:32.670
I did as you said, and thought really hard about Kyoto.
And after all that thinking, this is what I came up with.

10:37.130 --> 10:43.380
A better, smaller version of the self-sustaining
substitute mass-produced with my 3D printer!

10:43.830 --> 10:47.880
It doesn't need a spirit, just a substitute placed inside.

10:47.880 --> 10:51.000
It doesn't need to last long,
so we can use just water instead of gel,

10:51.580 --> 10:55.210
and the low viscosity of water
makes it repair itself even faster!

10:55.330 --> 10:59.750
And with this many substitutes,
our chance of surviving has never been higher!

10:59.750 --> 11:00.540
...been higher!

11:00.540 --> 11:01.250
...been higher!

11:01.250 --> 11:02.500
Yikes...

11:02.670 --> 11:05.670
What?! I thought you'd be way more excited!

11:05.880 --> 11:09.330
Ahem... You have certainly exceeded my expectations.

11:09.750 --> 11:15.500
But I can tell from this
that you're dead set on fighting by my side.

11:17.000 --> 11:20.670
You went to Kishimojin before,
trying to get rid of our curse, right?

11:21.210 --> 11:24.880
That must mean the curse was set on us
by something as powerful as a god.

11:25.790 --> 11:30.080
So I'd better be ready to take on
something as powerful as a god!

11:32.920 --> 11:34.460
Let's do this, Yayoi-chan!

11:34.880 --> 11:39.790
Thanks. You already do a lot for me,
but I'm gonna need you even more from here on out.

11:46.880 --> 11:51.580
The honest truth is I'm terrified.
I've been lucky to survive all this time.

11:51.710 --> 11:55.920
But things are gonna be
way more dangerous from here on out.

11:56.330 --> 11:57.420
I know that...

12:01.500 --> 12:05.290
...but I've already made my decision!

12:21.040 --> 12:24.960
I can't believe they're coming down
to see me! I can't wait!

12:39.080 --> 12:42.460
Wait, is this me? I'm, like, gorgeous!

12:42.830 --> 12:44.380
You look amazing, Ai.

12:44.960 --> 12:46.920
I knew you'd look wonderful.

12:46.920 --> 12:49.170
Mom! Auntie!

12:53.380 --> 12:55.210
Auntie?

12:55.380 --> 12:58.960
Didn't you die a long time ago?

13:07.580 --> 13:10.330
<b>SURGERY</b>

13:07.750 --> 13:10.080
The hospital? But why...

13:22.420 --> 13:24.330
Ai-chan...

13:25.630 --> 13:27.710
Auntie?

13:37.460 --> 13:38.500
What the-?

13:40.790 --> 13:42.000
Stop!

13:49.670 --> 13:51.040
Stop!

13:52.210 --> 13:54.040
Please! Help me, Sen-

13:55.000 --> 14:00.830
Wait... Who was I going to say?

14:01.210 --> 14:02.710
Help me, Li-

14:04.170 --> 14:08.080
Who? What...?

14:10.880 --> 14:15.630
Wait... Why am I crying?

14:20.380 --> 14:24.790
Help me... Help me... Help me...

14:26.500 --> 14:33.210
I feel like I'm missing something important...

14:34.330 --> 14:38.000
Like I'm turning into... Something else.

14:48.170 --> 14:53.540
What? Is that my face? Being taken away?

14:55.130 --> 14:57.540
No, it's still here.

15:04.130 --> 15:08.290
It's almost your time, Ai.

15:24.880 --> 15:26.040
Just a nightmare...

15:32.880 --> 15:37.790
Sensei! Little Senpai! Eiko-chan!

15:40.000 --> 15:41.790
I'm so scared...

15:51.790 --> 15:53.080
Kei-kun!

15:55.290 --> 15:58.790
I was gonna go see Ai-chan regardless.

15:59.250 --> 16:04.790
That alone puts me in danger of getting killed,
so I might as well fight for a chance to survive.

16:05.460 --> 16:08.080
I'm not sure if any of these are going to help,

16:08.080 --> 16:13.420
but I brought all the charms
my Grandma gave me for protection!

16:14.170 --> 16:15.000
Keitaro...

16:15.210 --> 16:17.500
I also put this together.

16:20.080 --> 16:21.670
<b>Three hours later</b>

16:23.170 --> 16:26.630
All done! This is my Graduate Deployment Kit!

16:30.670 --> 16:36.540
If I work on the range a bit more,
we can seal and release our Graduates totally remotely.

16:36.880 --> 16:38.580
This'll make recovering them afterwards way easier, too.

16:38.750 --> 16:41.380
Ooh, let me help spruce up the electronics!

16:41.540 --> 16:43.210
I was hoping you would.

16:43.500 --> 16:47.250
This is absolutely something I want to have.
Thank you, Keitaro.

16:47.790 --> 16:51.920
Sure. We're going to be leaning on you
to handle most of the battling,

16:52.420 --> 16:54.920
but still, let's go save Ai-chan, together!

16:55.210 --> 16:56.540
Yeah!

16:57.330 --> 16:58.040
Next up...

17:08.790 --> 17:10.210
There we go.

17:21.290 --> 17:23.000
I've fulfilled my promise.

17:23.500 --> 17:26.460
We will be engaging in battle again in Kyoto.

17:27.170 --> 17:29.540
I'd like to entrust a crucial part of our plan to you.

17:34.920 --> 17:38.250
Next time, bring friends.

17:39.830 --> 17:42.920
I'll bring a different kind of sake next time
so we can all learn more.

17:47.380 --> 17:50.080
Negotiations and collection complete.

17:51.170 --> 17:51.920
Now...

17:54.460 --> 17:58.880
So this is your Graduate dorm!

17:59.420 --> 18:03.330
There's a man hanging in the doorway,
but you can ignore him. He's harmless.

18:04.000 --> 18:05.080
O-okay.

18:07.710 --> 18:10.040
We'll put a tracker on the right arm.

18:10.420 --> 18:12.540
The left arm, we'll take with us to Kyoto.

18:12.920 --> 18:14.880
Why the distinction?

18:15.460 --> 18:18.250
This one's the one the old lady was carrying.

18:16.750 --> 18:18.330
<b>MAY 5TH</b>

18:16.750 --> 18:23.460
<b>REPLACED</b>

18:18.330 --> 18:23.460
<b>MAY 6TH</b>

18:18.790 --> 18:23.460
Right after that, another one of the body-snatchers
made contact with me.

18:24.080 --> 18:29.380
Since the two of them know each other,
they'll probably share information,

18:24.710 --> 18:26.040
<b>BODY-SNATCHERS</b>

18:28.670 --> 18:31.920
<b>THEY STOLE IT?!</b>

18:29.380 --> 18:34.040
so they'll likely come to try and take the right arm back.

18:31.920 --> 18:34.920
<b>LET'S GET IT BACK!</b>

18:35.210 --> 18:39.920
But they don't know we have the left arm.

18:40.670 --> 18:44.960
They might not come looking for the right arm,
but if they do, all the better for us,

18:44.960 --> 18:46.880
because then we'll know more about them.

18:47.250 --> 18:48.420
That makes sense.

18:52.790 --> 18:53.710
That'll do it.

18:55.080 --> 19:01.290
So that grade schooler likely has our arm.
Should we not go and take it from her?

19:01.500 --> 19:07.580
Though Dorothy says she is our brethren,
we do not yet know the truth for certain.

19:07.580 --> 19:10.080
We must observe her fully before taking rash action.

19:11.040 --> 19:13.250
What are you two talking about in here?

19:13.960 --> 19:18.330
Oh, we're discussing the friend you told us about.

19:19.500 --> 19:22.580
I knew the two of you would be
completely intrigued by her!

19:22.710 --> 19:28.880
Well, I'm only interested in the arm.
I can't speak for Nankobo-san over here, though.

19:31.290 --> 19:34.130
How fares the spirit, then?

19:35.500 --> 19:39.960
It's growing steadily, though it is still lacking in strength.

19:40.880 --> 19:45.790
That was quite the pinch, there.
We could have lost it for good.

19:46.040 --> 19:48.290
Should we go and lend it assistance?

19:51.040 --> 19:52.710
Would you?

19:52.960 --> 19:54.290
Right away.

19:54.290 --> 19:56.290
I'd like to come with you!

19:57.210 --> 20:00.750
That's the whole reason why I got school put on hold.

20:03.380 --> 20:06.330
We can also use it as an opportunity
to tour the great city of Kyoto!

20:06.330 --> 20:08.580
I am sure you know, but it bears repeating:

20:09.630 --> 20:12.330
do not make contact with that god.

20:13.130 --> 20:20.420
Of course we won't. I'm not so crazy
as to tangle with divinity, knock on wood.

20:22.420 --> 20:26.460
The cameras are set up, and we're prepped
to deal with any body-snatchers.

20:27.500 --> 20:28.380
Now...

20:29.170 --> 20:30.630
...we're ready.

20:32.830 --> 20:35.750
To Kyoto, then.

20:36.380 --> 20:37.670
Let's ghooo...

20:37.670 --> 20:39.330
...ooost!

20:42.830 --> 20:48.920
Oh right, Yayoi-chan, did you want to stop by the site
of the train accident? It's on the way.

20:50.500 --> 20:58.790
The Spectre was there... The spirit that killed her parents.
She could learn something from what happened there.

